  "{\n  \"AND\": {\n    \"left\": {\n      \"AND\": {\n        \"left\": {\n          \"raw_text\": \"-Patients residing in the following clinical states with a rising PSA: Patients with a history of localized disease who have undergone definitive radiation or surgery. These patients must demonstrate progression of disease biochemically as outlined below. Patients in this group may not have radiographically evident disease.\"\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw_text\": \"B. Non-castrate metastatic: Patients must present with radiographic evidence of metastatic disease at the time of diagnosis or after treatment for localized disease. These patients must show newly detected disease or progressing disease in bone or in soft tissue. Biochemical progression is defined as: minimum no. of determinations: 3 Interval: >2 weeks Minimal Baseline PSA value (ng/ml): 2 Minimal % increase in range of values: 50%\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"raw_text\": \"Diagnosis of prostate adenocarcinoma histologically confirmed at MSKCC.\"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"OR\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw_text\": \"Patient must have level of serum testosterone above the lower limit of normal.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"AND\": {\n                    \"left\": {\n                      \"raw_text\": \"Karnofsky performance status (KPS) >_70%.\"\n                    },\n                    \"right\": {\n                      \"AND\": {\n                        \"left\": {\n                          \"raw_text\": \"Patients must have adequate organ function as defined by the following laboratory criteria: WBC >_3500/mm3, platelet count >_100,000/mm3. Bilirubin <2.0 mg/dl or SGOT <3.0 X the upper limit of normal. Creatinine <_1.6 mg/dl or creatinine clearance >_60 cc/min.\"\n                        }\n                      }\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}" 

