  "{\n  \"AND\": {\n    \"left\": {\n      \"AND\": {\n        \"left\": {\n          \"raw_text\": \"1. Age: 12 to 36 months of age (The diagnosis of CP is often uncertain under the age of 12 months. The cutoff at 36 months is to have a population of young children when the brain is most \"plastic\" and most susceptible to reorganization).\"\n        },\n        \"right\": {\n          \"AND\": {\n            \"left\": {\n              \"raw_text\": \"2. Diagnosis: Diagnosis of spastic CP confirmed by a pediatric neurologist or pediatric rehabilitation specialist.\"\n            },\n            \"right\": {\n              \"AND\": {\n                \"left\": {\n                  \"raw_text\": \"3. Etiology: The insult to the central nervous system that caused the motor dysfunction must have occurred during gestation or within one year after birth independent of gestational age.\"\n                },\n                \"right\": {\n                  \"AND\": {\n                    \"left\": {\n                      \"raw_text\": \"4. Disease severity level: Gross Motor Function Classification System (GMFCS) levels I, II and III.\"\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n    }\n  }\n}" 

